More interactive USD edits of meshes, with the usd procedural cache_id and with the render delegate

A cube mesh has its subdivision scheme and corner sharpness edited. Two quads get a geom subset bound to another
material, whose indices change before it's removed, have their orientation, doubleSided and
primvars:arnold:visibility:camera edited, are bound to a material reading a primvar that's added, edited and removed,
and have authored normals added, edited and removed. The stage is re-rendered after each edit.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural (hydra reader) reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive
render session, and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the procedural render of step 4 is
compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues
in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
